# Mirrors the check list in .clangd's Diagnostics.ClangTidy section, so clang-tidy on the
# command line (via `make static-analysis`) agrees with what clangd shows live in the editor.
# Keep the two in sync when either changes.
#
# The checks below are disabled specifically because Zephyr's LOG_INF/LOG_ERR/LOG_WRN and
# LOG_MODULE_DECLARE/LOG_MODULE_REGISTER macros expand into internal cbprintf-packaging code
# (a variable-length array, do-while wrappers, vararg forwarding, C-style casts, dozens of locals
# that could be const, ...) that clang-tidy attributes to the macro's call site in our file, not
# to Zephyr's own headers - every one of these checks fires purely from that expansion, with zero
# real findings from code we actually wrote, and would otherwise fire on every LOG_* call in the
# codebase. (cppcoreguidelines-avoid-c-arrays/modernize-avoid-c-arrays did also catch one genuine
# C-array - matter_thread_adapter.h's m_identifyClusters - fixed by switching to std::array before
# these were disabled; if you add a new C-style array, clangd/clang-tidy won't warn about it.)
# cppcoreguidelines-avoid-non-const-global-variables is a partial exception (it also flags the
# macros' internal globals) - kept enabled since it also catches genuine globals (see the targeted
# NOLINT on button_adapter.cpp's s_pButtonAdapter and on each LOG_MODULE_* line).
#
# clang-analyzer-optin.cplusplus.UninitializedObject is disabled separately: unlike regular
# clang-tidy checks, its path-sensitive findings don't respect HeaderFilterRegex below, so it can
# report directly against a vendor header's own file:line even though nothing in src/ is involved
# (seen flagging Matter SDK's ConcreteClusterPath - its own comment says the field is deliberately
# left uninitialized). Not something we can fix or should suppress per-call-site.
Checks: >
  bugprone-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  concurrency-*,
  cppcoreguidelines-*,
  misc-*,
  modernize-*,
  performance-*,
  portability-*,
  readability-*,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-array-to-pointer-decay,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-bounds-pointer-arithmetic,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-reinterpret-cast,
  -modernize-use-trailing-return-type,
  -performance-avoid-endl,
  -misc-include-cleaner,
  -modernize-use-integer-sign-comparison,
  -modernize-use-ranges,
  -misc-const-correctness,
  -misc-redundant-expression,
  -misc-use-anonymous-namespace,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-do-while,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-vararg,
  -cppcoreguidelines-pro-type-cstyle-cast,
  -cppcoreguidelines-avoid-c-arrays,
  -modernize-avoid-c-arrays,
  -readability-simplify-boolean-expr,
  -readability-function-cognitive-complexity,
  -readability-function-size,
  -clang-analyzer-optin.cplusplus.UninitializedObject
WarningsAsErrors: ''
HeaderFilterRegex: '^src/'
FormatStyle: none
